   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-20",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker supported the Aboriginal Land Rights and Other Legislation Amendment Bill 2013, noting that the Northern Territory government, Northern Land Council, and local Aboriginal land trust back the scheduling of three land parcels, and that ERA seeks to avoid a painful native title negotiation. The speaker commended the parties for agreeing to reschedule the township of Jabiru under the act, despite criticism from others."
